==Teams==
A total of 18 teams will be contesting the league, including 12 sides from the [[2024–25 Saudi First Division League|2024–25 season]], the three promoted teams from the [[2024–25 Saudi Second Division League|Second Division]] and the three relegated sides from the [[2024–25 Saudi Pro League|Saudi Pro League]].

[[Al-Raed FC|Al-Raed]] were the first team to be relegated following a 1–0 defeat away to [[Damac FC|Damac]] on 11 May 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=رياضي / الرائد يهبط لدوري الدرجة الأولى |url=https://www.spa.gov.sa/760102}}</ref> Al-Raed were relegated after 17 consecutive seasons in the flight. On 25 May 2025, [[Al-Orobah FC|Al-Orobah]] became the second team to be relegated after they were docked three points for fielding an ineligible player against [[Al-Nassr FC|Al-Nassr]].<ref>{{cite web |title=النصر ينتزع نقاط العروبة بقرار مركز التحكيم |url=https://www.alarabiya.net/sport/2025/05/26/%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%86%D8%B5%D8%B1-%D9%8A%D9%86%D8%AA%D8%B2%D8%B9-%D9%86%D9%82%D8%A7%D8%B7-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D8%B1%D9%88%D8%A8%D8%A9-%D8%A8%D9%82%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%B1-%D9%85%D8%B1%D9%83%D8%B2-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AA%D8%AD%D9%83%D9%8A%D9%85}}</ref> Al-Orobah were relegated after one season in the top flight. [[Al Wehda FC|Al-Wehda]] were the third and final club to be relegated, following a 2–1 away defeat to [[Al-Ettifaq FC|Al-Ettifaq]] on the final matchday.<ref>{{cite web |title=الأخدود ينجو بريمونتادا مثيرة.. والوحدة يهبط |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/867044}}</ref> Al-Wehda were relegated after three seasons in the top flight. Al-Raed will play in their 17th season in the FD League, while Al-Orobah will play in their 16th season and Al-Wehda in their 10th season.

The first club to be promoted was [[Al-Diriyah Club|Al-Diriyah]] who did so after a 1–0 away win against [[Jerash FC|Jerash]] on 10 February 2025.<ref>{{cite web |title=الدرعية أول الصاعدين إلى دوري يلو.. |url=https://www.al-jazirah.com/2025/20250211/sp9.htm}}</ref> On 14 March 2025, [[Al-Ula FC|Al-Ula]] became the second club to be promoted following a 6–0 away win against [[Bisha FC|Bisha]].<ref>{{cite web |title=العُلا.. حكاية صعود تاريخي |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/862285}}</ref> The third and final club to be promoted was [[Al-Anwar Club|Al-Anwar]], who did so after defeating [[Al-Jeel Club|Al-Jeel]] 3–1 on penalties (1–1 after extra time) in the promotion play-off final.<ref>{{cite web |title=(الأنوار) يصعد إلى دوري (يلو) لأول مرة في تاريخه |url=https://www.al-jazirah.com/2025/20250414/sp4.htm}}</ref>

Al-Diriyah were crowned champions for the second time after defeating Al-Ula 1–0 in the final.<ref>{{cite web |title=الدرعية بطل دوري الدرجة الثانية |url=https://arriyadiyah.com/864286}}</ref>

Al-Diriyah return to the [[Saudi First Division League|First Division League]] after an absence of three years. They return to the league for the first time since the 2021–22 season and will play in their 6th overall season. Both Al-Anwar and Al-Ula were promoted to the First Division League for the first time in history.

